// offset_first_layer regression (ref 21 Aug 2026) -- the FIRST committed
// input exercising a radial domain offset: a brush grafted onto a
// cylindrical fibre of core radius 3 (the offset models the hard core;
// layer 1 spans r = 3..4), fjc = 1. Committed together with the
// offset-inclusive .pro coordinate column (the x column is the PHYSICAL
// radius offset + z - 0.5 = 3.5, 4.5, ..., matching Namics
// LGrad1.cpp:243 and PySFBox's own N-D radial axes; before 21 Aug 2026
// the 1-gradient writer omitted the offset). ORACLE-VALIDATED at
// creation against ../Namics/bin/namics on this input: kal
// theta/theta_exc/1st_M/F/GP at the convergence floor and the .pro
// byte-level convention match (coordinate column identical, profiles at
// the floor) -- at fjc = 1 the offset is handled consistently by both
// engines (the offset+fjc>1 combination is where they diverge: Namics
// places refined shells at fjc x the declared offset, reported
// upstream; see tests/manual/curved_fjc_excess.py for PySFBox's own
// offset+fjc consistency guards). Also guards the initial_guess:file
// offset round-trip (tests/manual/guess_file_guards.py seeds from this
// class of .pro).
lat : NN : n_layers : 30
lat : NN : geometry : cylindrical
lat : NN : lattice_type : simple_cubic
lat : NN : offset_first_layer : 3

mon : P : freedom : pinned
mon : P : pinned_range : 1;1
mon : A : freedom : free
mon : A : chi_W : 0.4
mon : W : freedom : free

mol : pol : composition : (P)1(A)29
mol : pol : freedom : restricted
mol : pol : theta : 60

mol : W : composition : (W)1
mol : W : freedom : solvent

newton : NN : tolerance : 1e-8

output : kal : append : false
kal : mol : pol : theta
kal : mol : pol : theta_exc
kal : mon : A : 1st_M_phi_z
kal : sys : NN : free_energy
kal : sys : NN : grand_potential

output : pro : append : false
pro : mon : A : phi
pro : mol : pol : phi

start
